# Help: Standalone module-init runtime test suites
#
# The Runtime Testing menu entries that are neither KUnit suites nor
# driven by a kselftest collection: classic test modules whose init
# runs the whole suite at load, so loading the module is the run and
# the load's exit status (plus the kernel log) is the verdict. The
# exit conventions differ per module by upstream design: the XArray,
# Maple Tree, rhashtable, hexdump and BPF suites return
# nonzero on failure; the rbtree, interval-tree, percpu, workqueue
# and vmalloc suites always return -EAGAIN so the module never stays
# loaded, reporting failures only through kernel WARNINGs; the IDA
# suite inverts the convention (-EINVAL on success, same auto-unload
# idiom); atomic64 BUGs on failure; find_bit and dhrystone are
# benchmarks.
#
# Prerequisites inlined per the self-containment rule: DEBUG_KERNEL
# gates the rbtree, interval-tree and percpu tests; NET gates
# TEST_BPF; RUNTIME_TESTING_MENU gates the whole menu. Every suite is
# loaded on demand by the test harness; no builtin/ counterpart
# needed. Deliberate omissions: LKDTM crashes the kernel by design,
# and TEST_PARMAN is unreachable without COMPILE_TEST (the PARMAN
# library it exercises is promptable only there), which has no place
# in a bootable kernel.
# See: lib/Kconfig.debug (menu "Runtime Testing")

CONFIG_RUNTIME_TESTING_MENU=y
CONFIG_DEBUG_KERNEL=y
CONFIG_NET=y

CONFIG_TEST_XARRAY=m
CONFIG_TEST_MAPLE_TREE=m
CONFIG_TEST_RHASHTABLE=m
CONFIG_TEST_IDA=m
CONFIG_TEST_HEXDUMP=m
CONFIG_TEST_BPF=m
CONFIG_RBTREE_TEST=m
CONFIG_INTERVAL_TREE_TEST=m
CONFIG_PERCPU_TEST=m
CONFIG_TEST_WORKQUEUE=m
CONFIG_TEST_VMALLOC=m
CONFIG_ATOMIC64_SELFTEST=m
CONFIG_FIND_BIT_BENCHMARK=m
CONFIG_TEST_DHRY=m
